# What not to upload to Vercel.
#
# Vercel only builds the client bundle here, so everything else is dead weight -
# and two of these actively break the upload on Windows:
#
#   .mongo-data/  WiredTiger files held open by a running local mongod, which
#                 makes the CLI fail with "EBUSY: resource busy or locked"
#   node_modules/ reinstalled on Vercel anyway; uploading it is slow and pointless

.mongo-data/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
client/dist/
.git/
.env
.env.*
*.log

# Server-side code. The API runs elsewhere - it needs a long-lived process for
# the WebSocket hub's change streams and the offline-sweep timer.
server/

# Local-only tooling and docs.
scripts/
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
render.yaml
DEPLOY.md
WORKBOOK.html
